 {success}←parms HandleLX(ref2TatinVars ref2project);ns;success;rc;msg
⍝ Returns 1 in case a package parameter "lx" was successfully executed and 0 otherwise.
 success←0
 :If ref2TatinVars≢⎕NULL
     ns←⎕JSON⍠('Dialect' 'JSON5')⊢ref2TatinVars.CONFIG
 :AndIf 0<ns.⎕NC'lx'
 :AndIf 0<≢ns.lx
     :If parms.batch
     :OrIf 1 C.YesOrNo'ExecLX@lx←',ns.lx,'  -- execute?'
         (success rc msg)←ExecUnderTrap(⍕ref2project),'.',parms.projectSpace,'.',ns.lx
         :If ~success
             ∆Problems+←1
⍝ `msg` is `⎕DM` as `ExecUnderTrap` returned it - three lines, and the only statement anywhere of what
⍝ actually went wrong. It used to be overwritten by the headline, which then built its detail out of
⍝ the overwritten value, so the user was told that something had failed and never what.
             msg←(⊂'>>> Executing "lx" (according to the package conf) caused an error:'),(⊂'    RC=',⍕rc),(⊂4⍴' '),¨msg
             msg←1↓⊃,/CR,¨msg
             msg Assert~parms.batch
             1 PrintToSession msg
         :EndIf
     :EndIf
 :EndIf
⍝Done
